  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nHigh pressure continues to influence the region through Saturday \nwith seasonable temperatures expected. A shortwave aloft will swing \neast across the Upper Ohio Valley during the afternoon and evening \nhours today. The majority of the area should remain dry but have \nintroduced low-end rain chances along and south of US-30 later today \nfor any isolated showers that may develop. Isolated showers and \nstorms are expected along and east of I-77 Saturday morning and \nafternoon as mid-level moisture increases. \n\nHigh temperatures will rise into the low 80s today and Saturday. \nOvernight lows in the upper 50s to lower 60s tonight with warmer \nlows in the mid 60s Saturday night.  \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2... \nActive weather is expected to return early next week as a ridge over \nthe western United States builds and allows for a trough to dig \nsouth across the the Great Lakes region. Surface low pressure will \nusher in a strong LLJ over a moist airmass with dew points in the \nupper 60s. This will increase the potential for clusters of \nthunderstorms. Strong to severe storms remain possible, particularly \non Monday, as highlighted by the SPC Severe Risk area. Shower and \nthunderstorm chances linger into mid-week as the aforementioned low \npushes east across the Lower Great Lakes. A fair amount of \nuncertainty remains in timing, coverage, and intensity of storms \ngiven the conditional nature of this setup.",
